  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Paragon Systems has $342M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Paragon Systems received 254 awards in the current fiscal year to date, with an average award size of $1.3M. Paragon Systems obligations are down 42.8% year over year. Historical annual obligations show Paragon Systems at $634M in FY21, $595M in FY22, $669M in FY23, $617M in FY24, and $598M in FY25. Paragon Systems has concentrated buying from the Department of Homeland Security at $279M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $38.4M and the Department of Justice at $23M. Paragon Systems sells primarily in Security Guards and Patrol Services at $302M and Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) at $40.1M. The current-year totals are partial because the period is fiscal year to date, and the note clarifies that the listed largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables show total contract values while other figures are contract obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Paragon Systems' top federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Homeland Security is the largest customer at $279M. The Department of Health and Human Services follows at $38.4M, and the Department of Justice follows at $23M. The National Archives and Records Administration and the Department of Defense also appear among top buyers at $1.2M and $820K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Paragon Systems' federal work?",
        "body": "Security Guards and Patrol Services is the largest market at $302M. Security Systems Services (except Locksmiths) is the next market at $40.1M. These two markets account for the bulk of Paragon Systems' FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
